---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../site.js";
---
<Base title="Greeneville AI Meetup: What AI Can Do for You" description="A free evening to learn what AI can do for you, from first steps to deep technical dives, with hands-on help and plenty of time for questions. Thursday, November 12, 2026, 7–9pm, Greeneville/Greene County Public Library.">
  <article class="meetup">
    <p class="eyebrow">Free community meetup · Greeneville, Tennessee</p>
    <h1>Greeneville AI Meetup</h1>
    <p class="sub">An evening to learn what AI can do for you, from your first question to AI agents that do real work. Beginners are especially welcome.</p>

    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>When</dt><dd>Thursday, November 12, 2026, 7–9pm</dd>
      <dt>Where</dt><dd>Big Spring Room, Greeneville/Greene County Public Library<br><a href="https://maps.google.com/?q=210+N+Main+St,+Greeneville,+TN+37745">210 N Main St, Greeneville</a></dd>
      <dt>Cost</dt><dd>Free and open to everyone</dd>
    </dl>

    <div class="actions">
      <a class="cta primary" href="/meetup/signup/">Get event news</a>
      <a class="cta" href="/meetup/slides/">Slides</a>
      <a class="cta" href="/greeneville-ai-meetup.ics">Add to calendar</a>
    </div>

    <h2>What we'll cover</h2>
    <ul class="topics">
      <li><strong>Chatbots</strong><span>Asking ChatGPT and Claude for help with writing, research, planning and everyday questions.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Agents</strong><span>Tools like Claude Code and Codex that don't just answer, but do the work for you.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Try it yourself</strong><span>Bring a phone or laptop if you have one, and get help as you go. Optional.</span></li>
      <li><strong>The deep end</strong><span>A live look at how AI agents build real software, and how to check their work.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Questions</strong><span>Ask anything, at any level, all evening.</span></li>
      <li><strong>No experience needed</strong><span>Whatever your age or background, you're welcome.</span></li>
    </ul>

    <section class="signup" id="event-news">
      <h2>Get Millillion event news</h2>
      <p>Hear about the next Greeneville AI Meetup, other meetups, conferences and anything else Millillion hosts.</p>
      <p id="joined" class="notice" hidden>Thank you. You're on the list.</p>
      <p id="join-error" class="notice" hidden>Sorry, that didn't go through. Please check your email address and try again.</p>
      <form class="signup-form" method="post" action="/api/events">
        <label>Name <input name="name" required maxlength="200" autocomplete="name" /></label>
        <label>Email <input name="email" type="email" required maxlength="200" autocomplete="email" /></label>
        <input type="hidden" name="source" value="meetup page" />
        <label class="hp" aria-hidden="true">Company <input name="company" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" /></label>
        <button class="cta primary" type="submit">Sign up</button>
      </form>
    </section>

    <section class="host">
      <h2>Your host</h2>
      <p><strong>Jordan Last</strong>, an agentic engineer with an emphasis in software development, and the founder of <a href="/">Millillion</a>.</p>
      <p class="contact">Questions? <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> · <a href={`tel:${SITE.phone.replace(/-/g, "")}`}>{SITE.phone}</a></p>
    </section>

    <p class="fine">The meetup is held at the library; it isn't a library-sponsored program.</p>
  </article>
  <script is:inline>
    const q = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
    if (q.has("joined")) document.getElementById("joined").hidden = false;
    if (q.has("error")) document.getElementById("join-error").hidden = false;
  </script>
</Base>
